+# Retention planning: summary
+
+## What changed
+
+- `vaultsnap/retention.py`: implemented `plan_retention(snapshots, policy, now)`. It only plans and deletes nothing. `Plan` and the signature are unchanged. Zone offset tables from ADR-0005 are in this file.
+- `tests/test_retention_adr.py` (new): 22 tests for the rules the original `tests/test_retention.py` does not reach. `tests/test_retention.py` is unchanged.
+
+## Which records apply
+
+Status lines were read for all ten records. The index in `docs/adr/README.md` is stale: it stops at 0007, and it says it is not updated when later records amend older ones.
+
+| Part of the policy | Record(s) applied | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| Inputs: naive datetimes, duplicate ids, parent checks | ADR-0001, ADR-0007 | Stated in the record |
+| Ordering (ties broken by greater id) | ADR-0001 | Stated in the record |
+| Protected, later-than-now (set aside) | ADR-0001, ADR-0008 lines 1–2 | Order of overrides |
+| Expired (pruned, line 3) | ADR-0008 | Order of overrides |
+| Window `keep_within_hours` (set aside, line 4) | ADR-0006 (definition), ADR-0009 (set aside, not counted) | ADR-0009 reverts ADR-0006's bucket interaction |
+| `keep_last` | ADR-0001 | Stated in the record |
+| Daily / yearly buckets | ADR-0001, ADR-0004 (day boundary), ADR-0005 (zones) | Bucket time from offset and `day_start_hour` |
+| Weekly buckets | ADR-0003 (ISO weeks) | Replaces the Sunday-start rule of ADR-0001 |
+| Monthly buckets | ADR-0001, ADR-0010 (`month_start_day`) | Amends the monthly row only |
+| Empty policy | ADR-0001 as amended by ADR-0006 (six rules), ADR-0008 | Expired still pruned |
+| Parent hold (dependency step) | ADR-0007 | Runs last, overrides expired |
+| Output | ADR-0001, extended by ADR-0007–0009 | Each list newest first |
+
+### Not in force (deliberately not implemented)
+
+- ADR-0002 (UTC buckets): superseded by ADR-0004.
+- ADR-0001 "Weeks" (Sunday start): superseded by ADR-0003.
+- ADR-0004's sentence "no daylight saving handling and no zone names": superseded by ADR-0005.
+- ADR-0006 "Interaction with the bucket rules" (window snapshots count toward N): reverted by ADR-0009.
+- ADR-0001 "five rules": amended to six by ADR-0006.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `python -m unittest` → `Ran 29 tests ... OK` (7 original, 22 new). Before the change: 7 errors (`NotImplementedError`).
+- `python -m py_compile vaultsnap/retention.py tests/test_retention_adr.py` → compiled.
+- `git status` shows only `vaultsnap/retention.py`, `tests/test_retention_adr.py`, and `SUMMARY.md`.
+- One new test failed on my first run because of a mistake in the test (its snapshots were later than the test's `now`). I fixed the test, not the code, and the fix follows ADR-0001.
+
+## Not verified / uncertain
+
+- **Keep-within alone:** a policy with only `keep_within_hours` set prunes everything outside the window. I read ADR-0006's "all six rules off" as the only case that keeps everything. Please confirm this is what you want.
+- **Zone tables:** I transcribed the ADR-0005 tables by hand. Tests check only the switch instants and a few dates. I did not diff them against a second source.
+- **CI:** the repo has no CI config that I could read, so I could not confirm the CI command beyond your description. Nothing was run against real snapshots or the nightly job.
+- **Stale docs, outside my allowed edits:** `docs/adr/README.md` omits 0008–0010, so its table does not show the current status of ADR-0001 (amended in parts) or ADR-0004 (one sentence superseded). The README retention section is an old draft (you said so). Both should be updated; I did not change them.
